---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout title="Refund Policy" updated="October 7, 2026">
  <p>
    This Refund Policy applies to users who purchase the Ekwly Pro subscription or any other paid
    digital goods within the Ekwly application.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Subscription Cancellations</h2>
  <p>
    Ekwly Pro is a recurring digital subscription. You may cancel your subscription at any time
    through your account settings or your app store provider. Upon cancellation, you will retain
    access to Ekwly Pro features until the end of your current paid billing cycle.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Refund Eligibility</h2>
  <p>
    Because Ekwly incurs immediate hard costs for AI processing (Magic Scans) the moment they are
    used, our refund policy is strictly governed by usage:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Unused Subscriptions:</strong> If you are charged for a new billing cycle and request
      a refund within <strong>7 days</strong>, provided you have not utilized any Pro features
      (including unlimited Magic Scans) during that period, we will issue a full refund.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Used Subscriptions:</strong> If you have utilized Magic Scans or generated Analytics
      reports during the current billing cycle, you are <strong>not eligible</strong> for a refund
      for that month.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Technical Failures</h2>
  <p>
    If you experience a severe technical failure that prevents you from using the core features of
    Ekwly Pro for an extended period, please contact support. Refunds or account credits for
    downtime are evaluated on a case-by-case basis.
  </p>

  <h2>4. How to Request a Refund</h2>
  <p>
    To request an eligible refund, please email <strong>billing@ekwly.com</strong> with your Ekwly
    account email and the receipt of your transaction. Please allow 5-7 business days for the refund
    to be processed by your financial institution.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
